,"position":"1787814659190477001-f0ed7891-ba1d-459b-9617-e296441dd7fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-247_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"41c69740-e628-4506-a328-65f32258a98e","close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787805898239381001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c6920807-d58f-48e4-803f-c116ad1fff8c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"cf34-9b8b-1aa7-4d95"},{"link_uuid":"78028bcf-b2d0-4e7c-a066-f3292b28978d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4805-1df8-f846-4cf6"},{"link_uuid":"c7bd3ee0-2a4e-4365-a6f4-30755d6e4321","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"15bb-67fe-da53-462d"},{"link_uuid":"28cfd984-1521-4382-b8cf-d5bb793199c9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dd68-9c80-ca3d-4002"},{"link_uuid":"d69d7eca-a4fd-438c-84f7-df9aa96bffb7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c492-4faa-9d94-42c8"},{"link_uuid":"6efc9222-8e6a-465d-94b9-9bf6311f295e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"31a9-0b0e-1f77-40e1"},{"link_uuid":"f0ed7891-ba1d-459b-9617-e296441dd7fb","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"6964-40bb-46c9-48a7"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`autodeploy.sh` keeps ONE piece of global state for TWO independently-deploying components (the\nreview-bot and the mcp blue-green target). Split out of `cf34-9b8b-1aa7-4d95` with the\noperator's approval: that ticket scopes the review-bot DEFERRAL so control reaches the mcp\nblock; this one makes the state each component depends on per-component.\n\nFour rounds of code review on the combined change each found the same defect shape, each fix\nexposing the next. They are one concern and belong in one ticket.\n\n## The three couplings\n\n**Completion.** `deployed-sha` is written once, at the footer, so ANY early exit loses the\ncompletion of whichever component DID deploy, and the next tick redeploys it. A review-bot\nredeploy stop-and-drains the container, killing an in-flight review (bug 34cd) — the exact\nharm the drain gate exists to prevent, arriving from the other direction.\n\n**Failure.** `record_backoff_failure` writes ONE `deploy-backoff` keyed on the global `$TARGET`,\nand the top-level gate exits the whole script on it. On `main` it is called from BOTH blocks\n(~5 sites in the bot block, ~10 in the mcp block), so an mcp failure throttles the BOT and a\nbot failure suppresses mcp.\n\n**Incompleteness.** A component skipped by an open backoff window has not deployed, but nothing\nrecords that, so the footer stamps `$TARGET` into its marker for a deploy that never ran. The\nnext tick then computes no delta and drops the pending change PERMANENTLY.\n\n## Shape of the fix\n\n- `mcp-deployed-sha` and `bot-deployed-sha`, each written the moment that component completes,\n  with each component's delta gate RE-POINTED to diff from its own marker rather than the\n  global `$DEPLOYED` baseline. An absent or unparseable marker falls back to `$DEPLOYED`.\n  The global `deployed-sha` KEEPS its existing role unchanged: it is the TICK-level record,\n  advanced only at the footer and only on a tick that completed, and it still drives the\n  top-level \"up to date; no-op\" early exit (`if [ \"$TARGET\" = \"$DEPLOYED\" ]`). It is not\n  removed and not split — the component markers are added ALONGSIDE it. On a complete tick the\n  footer ALSO stamps both component markers. Those two writes are not in conflict: the\n  mid-tick write records a component that actually DEPLOYED, and the footer write is an\n  idempotent top-up covering the component that was a NO-OP this tick (nothing changed under\n  its trigger paths), so it is never left behind the global marker. For a component that\n  already deployed, the footer rewrites the same value. On an INCOMPLETE tick the guard exits\n  before the footer, so the only markers written are the mid-tick ones for components that\n  genuinely deployed — which is precisely the asymmetry per-component state exists to record. `$DEPLOYED` also remains the fallback baseline for a component whose marker is\n  absent or unparseable, which is what makes the first tick after upgrade behave as today.\n\n- A separate `mcp-deploy-backoff` recorder; the existing file then records bot failures only,\n  which is what makes it safe to move its gate off the top of the script. Each gate sits with\n  the component it throttles and skips that component instead of exiting the tick.\n- `bot_incomplete` / `mcp_incomplete`, honoured by the footer guard, so a backoff-skip with a\n  delta still pending never records completion. Each gate tests the DELTA before the window, so\n  \"nothing to do\" stays distinguishable from \"skipped with work pending\".\n- Both recorders keep emitting the `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` marker. That token — not the reason\n  string — is what the alarm counts: `infra/scripts/observability.sh:230` does a bare\n  `grep -cE '^AUTODEPLOY_ERROR \\{'` over the unit journal and publishes the count as\n  `rebar/host:deploy_errors` (`:240`, §4d). It never parses the reason, so alarm continuity is\n  preserved by continuing to emit the marker at all. The reason stays `deploy_failed` and\n  gains a `component=mcp` marker for OPERATOR legibility — telling the two paths apart when\n  reading the journal — not for the metric.\n\n## Consumers outside autodeploy.sh\n\nThe marker's only non-test consumer is `infra/scripts/observability.sh` (§4d, lines 230/240),\nwhich counts `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` occurrences into `rebar/host:deploy_errors`. It is deliberately\nkept distinct from the deferral and retire-cap tokens (`:259-260`, `:282`, `:338`) so routine\ndeferrals and retire-caps never inflate that alarm — this change adds no new token, so that\nseparation is unchanged. Test consumers of the marker: `test_autodeploy_review_drain.py`,\n`test_autodeploy_health_gate.py`, `test_observability_rotation_2dc7.py`,\n`test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py`.\n\nThe one test consumer of the shared STATE FILE is `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py:86`,\nwhich reads `state/deploy-backoff` after a REVIEW-BOT failure. That file keeps its name and\nkeeps recording bot failures, so the test needs no change and continues to pass unmodified —\nverified, 4 passed. Only the mcp block's failures move to the new file, and no existing test\nreads that path. Had the split renamed `deploy-backoff` instead of narrowing what writes to it,\nthis consumer would have broken silently; narrowing rather than renaming is what avoids that.\n\n## Boundary correction (2026-08-27)\n\nThe mcp completion marker (`mcp-deployed-sha` and re-pointing the mcp delta gate to it) has\nMOVED to `cf34-9b8b-1aa7-4d95`. Code review showed the original boundary was wrong: without\nthat marker, cf34's fix re-triggers a full blue-green cutover on every tick of a deferral\nepisode, so making the mcp path REACHABLE on a deferred tick and keeping it from redeploying\nevery deferred tick are one concern and belong in one change. This ticket keeps the BOT-side\nmarker, the scoped backoffs, and the incompleteness flags.\n\n## Deliberately out of scope\n\nA bot FATAL path still exits the tick, so mcp misses that single tick, after which the bot is in\nbackoff and skipped and mcp proceeds. Bounding it to one tick is enough; making the bot's fatal\npaths return rather than exit is a larger restructure of a live deploy script.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAll six mutation-checked: removing the behaviour each guards returns its test to RED.\n\n- [x] An mcp failure does not write the SHARED backoff.\n      Proof: `test_mcp_failure_on_a_deferred_tick_does_not_backoff_the_bot`\n- [x] An mcp failure does not cause the review-bot to redeploy on later ticks.\n      Proof: `test_a_failed_mcp_deploy_does_not_redeploy_the_bot_every_tick`\n- [x] A component skipped by its own backoff window is not recorded as deployed (both halves).\n      Proof: `test_bot_backoff_tick_does_not_record_the_bot_as_deployed`,\n      `test_mcp_backoff_tick_does_not_record_mcp_as_deployed`\n- [x] An open backoff window with NO pending delta is not reported as a skip.\n      Proof: `test_an_open_bot_backoff_with_no_pending_delta_is_not_reported_as_a_skip`\n- [x] An mcp backoff throttles mcp while the review-bot still deploys on the same tick.\n      Proof: `test_mcp_backoff_throttles_only_mcp_and_lets_the_bot_deploy` — mutating the mcp\n      recorder to also poison the shared backoff kills it on the bot assertion specifically.\n- [x] mcp failures still emit an `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` marker, so `deploy_errors`\n      (`observability.sh:230,240`) counts them as before, and the reason names `component=mcp`.\n      Proof: `test_mcp_failure_keeps_the_deploy_failed_metric_and_names_the_component`\n\n\n## Verification\n\n    .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/scripts/ -q -p no:randomly\n\nEach new test is mutation-checked: removing the behaviour it guards returns it to RED.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Per-component completion markers (mcp-deployed-sha, bot-deployed-sha) with each delta gate re-pointed to its own marker; an mcp-scoped backoff recorder and per-component gates; bot_incomplete/mcp_incomplete honoured by the footer guard"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"Mutation-checked coverage for each coupling: shared-backoff isolation, no bot redeploy after an mcp failure, neither component recorded as deployed when skipped by its own backoff, and metric continuity"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","15bb-67fe-da53-462d"],["relates_to","31a9-0b0e-1f77-40e1"],["relates_to","4805-1df8-f846-4cf6"],["relates_to","c492-4faa-9d94-42c8"],["relates_to","dd68-9c80-ca3d-4002"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"56332c28-e988-4394-a9b2-87236b27d475","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5774-fdb2-3d7f-4bab","ticket_type":"bug","title":"autodeploy keeps one global state for two independent components: per-component completion, backoff, and incompleteness","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b5bbacfd-1281-4f10-b44d-0dd8d464413b","b9d74139-5f59-4fd0-b759-8a6f36a6a40b","efd394e8-a458-45fc-b4d3-88b418792872","78028bcf-b2d0-4e7c-a066-f3292b28978d","fe5002ae-1615-4e9f-a0ff-96a8a3bb62c5","5786ab50-40e3-4ebc-b870-56a7e468daaf","c7bd3ee0-2a4e-4365-a6f4-30755d6e4321","1082e803-5ddb-457c-bb47-efd181365ca6","7ad451fe-e888-49a6-bb4f-36dce0660c99","28cfd984-1521-4382-b8cf-d5bb793199c9","d69d7eca-a4fd-438c-84f7-df9aa96bffb7","6efc9222-8e6a-465d-94b9-9bf6311f295e","e46a7177-6b19-4145-8f43-9ebd459033b1","56332c28-e988-4394-a9b2-87236b27d475","23702413-b020-482c-8b85-7836f73debbf","f0ed7891-ba1d-459b-9617-e296441dd7fb"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787821811037051431,"uuid":"1eaa1ef7-8557-4148-acc9-434259d93b25"}